Yes i do override. I started doing so for reason of `pdo_cassandra` driver rejecting my writes with errors.

Until today, it was called only on writes.

How should i modify it and/or any other methods ?

``` php
namespace app\components\cassandra;

use \PDO;

class ColumnSchema extends \yii\db\ColumnSchema {

    /** @var int ? Place in Cassandra clustering key, 0-based, null is partitioning key */
    public $componentIndex;

    /**
     * Solve problems of type-casting before writing to Cassandra, case by case
     *
     * Point of knowing both types
     *
     * @inheritdoc
     */
    public function typecast($value) {
        $value = parent::typecast($value);

        // Now convert single-value to tuple (value,PDO type)
        // according to Cassandra column type and value type
        if ( 'UTF8Type' === $this->dbType ) {
            $value = array( (string)$value, PDO::PARAM_STR );
        }

        return $value;
    }
} 
```

issue.body:
When using the binary bytea type in postgres the result of a data fetch will be a resource handle. Yii2 casts certain data type. It did not consider this special case and therefore casts the resource type to a string. This breaks handling blobs!

Not sure how blobs are handled in mysql or other dbs but chances are that it is not really a good idea to force a cast to a string...

```
namespace yii\db;
